      "content": "It's completely understandable to feel this way; what you're experiencing is often called the \"post-achievement void.\" After pouring a decade of your life into a singular goal, the sudden realization of having reached it can feel strangely empty. Allow yourself to feel that numbness, because it's your brain recalibrating after such intense effort. Perhaps this is the perfect moment to explore what comes next, outside of the climb itself.",
